(3316643, 461439, 45519, '<td valign="top">Aren''t watches always supposed to be set to 10:10 for photography? ;-)  Joking aside, it would enhance the image, IMO, if the hands on the time piece were in-fram versus just the second hand.  The fact the watch and dollar figures are in the same focal plane keeps drawing my eye back and forth between them (which might not be such a good thing, though your image is aptly titled!).  When landing on the watch it feels "cut off" because the hands are cropped out of the framing.  Still, nice execution of shallow DOF.</td>', 'Aren''t watches always supposed to be set to 10:10 for photography? ;-)  Joking aside, it would enhance the image, IMO, if the hands on the time piece were in-fram versus just the second hand.  The fact the watch and dollar figures are in the same focal plane keeps drawing my eye back and forth between them (which might not be such a good thing, though your image is aptly titled!).  When landing on the watch it feels "cut off" because the hands are cropped out of the framing.  Still, nice execution of shallow DOF.', '2007-02-01 23:47:13.000000', NULL, 1),
