(3339040, 459794, 62895, '<td valign="top">I didn''t see this one. There was a different one that I thought was yours, but this one is deffinately better.</td>', 'I didn''t see this one. There was a different one that I thought was yours, but this one is deffinately better.', '2007-02-07 10:54:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3339048, 461632, 5112, '<td valign="top">Judy, so this one was yours!  Love it.  I love pictures that "hint" at things, like the living place in back here - hints often say so much more than the real thing (like in the older movies, where instead of sex they would have stuff on the floor and music and whatever, and everybody KNEW what was going on, and your imagination took over).  That was just an example.  <br/> <br/>Technically the shallow DOF is just right (IMO).  Exposure wise, it seems a bit bright in the middle, in the windows/door of the house; the reflected same areas are fine, but the real ones are lost.  I think what probably made this not work quite as well as it could have is that the "hint" and the "hinted" do not have an obvious connection.  In other words, what does the little stick in front have to do with the dwelling place?  It''s like two separate things that are not connected in a obvious story way.<br/> <br/>So why am I writing a long comment.  I don''t know.  Just bored I guess :)</td>', 'Judy, so this one was yours!  Love it.  I love pictures that "hint" at things, like the living place in back here - hints often say so much more than the real thing (like in the older movies, where instead of sex they would have stuff on the floor and music and whatever, and everybody KNEW what was going on, and your imagination took over).  That was just an example.   Technically the shallow DOF is just right (IMO).  Exposure wise, it seems a bit bright in the middle, in the windows/door of the house; the reflected same areas are fine, but the real ones are lost.  I think what probably made this not work quite as well as it could have is that the "hint" and the "hinted" do not have an obvious connection.  In other words, what does the little stick in front have to do with the dwelling place?  It''s like two separate things that are not connected in a obvious story way. So why am I writing a long comment.  I don''t know.  Just bored I guess :)', '2007-02-07 10:56:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3339062, 461476, 5112, '<td valign="top">Ah, Nani, back to making picts I see.  :)  HI!!!!!</td>', 'Ah, Nani, back to making picts I see.  :)  HI!!!!!', '2007-02-07 10:59:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3339073, 461507, 67258, '<td valign="top">Brian, in the forum you asked for some feedback on this photo, so I shall try and articulate the reasons I gave it a 6.  The photo is a competent exploration of shallow depth of field, with both the near foreground and the background being thrown out of focus; this has isolated the subject, in the form of the King and Queen, well.  The composition is sound, roughly following the rule of thirds, although it is a little busy.  The title has gone completely over the top of my head, and ended up confusing me.   At the end of the day, it was the fact that I saw the photo as a good technical exercise, rather than an exciting picture that I wanted to view again, that prevented me from scoring higher than 6.  Hope this helps.</td>', 'Brian, in the forum you asked for some feedback on this photo, so I shall try and articulate the reasons I gave it a 6.  The photo is a competent exploration of shallow depth of field, with both the near foreground and the background being thrown out of focus; this has isolated the subject, in the form of the King and Queen, well.  The composition is sound, roughly following the rule of thirds, although it is a little busy.  The title has gone completely over the top of my head, and ended up confusing me.   At the end of the day, it was the fact that I saw the photo as a good technical exercise, rather than an exciting picture that I wanted to view again, that prevented me from scoring higher than 6.  Hope this helps.', '2007-02-07 11:02:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(3339075, 461324, 11960, '<td valign="top">Wow. I absolutely love this shot! Awesome job!</td>', 'Wow. I absolutely love this shot! Awesome job!', '2007-02-07 11:02:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3339079, 461507, 42198, '<td valign="top">Nice use of DOF. Although you''re not making the most of the tonal range. If you look at the levels histogram for this there''s a large unused area in the right (the white end of the histogram) so it doesn''t really ''pop''. The blacks (especially the background) aren''t pure black, and the whites aren''t pure white.<br/> <br/>I would have given this a 5 or a 6; technically it''s okay, but the subject and setup aren''t very interesting.</td>', 'Nice use of DOF. Although you''re not making the most of the tonal range. If you look at the levels histogram for this there''s a large unused area in the right (the white end of the histogram) so it doesn''t really ''pop''. The blacks (especially the background) aren''t pure black, and the whites aren''t pure white. I would have given this a 5 or a 6; technically it''s okay, but the subject and setup aren''t very interesting.', '2007-02-07 11:03:58.000000', NULL, 0);
