(3341160, 461153, 45559, '<td valign="top">Beautiful! I really would like to do some shooting with you some times. You rock!</td>', 'Beautiful! I really would like to do some shooting with you some times. You rock!', '2007-02-07 19:14:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341164, 459850, 7810, '<td valign="top">This shot was way underrated. Really liked this shot ... Love the lines</td>', 'This shot was way underrated. Really liked this shot ... Love the lines', '2007-02-07 19:16:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341206, 461298, 72778, '<td valign="top"><br/>Great shot Marcus.<br/> <br/>Nice to see an image I rate as number one in a challenge finally finish there.<br/> <br/>All the best,<br/>Ed</td>', 'Great shot Marcus. Nice to see an image I rate as number one in a challenge finally finish there. All the best,Ed', '2007-02-07 19:28:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341225, 458194, 66384, '<td valign="top">Good shot, wrong challenge.</td>', 'Good shot, wrong challenge.', '2007-02-07 19:34:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341269, 459473, 23484, '<td valign="top">Jason, I really like this shot and I''m surprised it didn''t do a little better than it did.  I was looking at this for a while trying to figure out what people didn''t care for. After-all, the needle is very clear and nicely framed by the sculpture. <br/> <br/>I''m just wondering if it''s because the out-of-focus part is in the foreground and the in-focus part is in the background instead of the other way around.  I think most shallow DOF shots are the opposite of what you have.  <br/> <br/>I don''t know if that was it but it was just a thought.<br/> <br/>By the way, I was up in that space needle in 1972 when I was stationed at PSNS for a while and I saw Led Zeppelin at the Seattle Center Coliseium (right near the space needle). At the time, it was called the Seattle Center.</td>', 'Jason, I really like this shot and I''m surprised it didn''t do a little better than it did.  I was looking at this for a while trying to figure out what people didn''t care for. After-all, the needle is very clear and nicely framed by the sculpture.  I''m just wondering if it''s because the out-of-focus part is in the foreground and the in-focus part is in the background instead of the other way around.  I think most shallow DOF shots are the opposite of what you have.   I don''t know if that was it but it was just a thought. By the way, I was up in that space needle in 1972 when I was stationed at PSNS for a while and I saw Led Zeppelin at the Seattle Center Coliseium (right near the space needle). At the time, it was called the Seattle Center.', '2007-02-07 19:46:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341350, 460457, 57060, '<td valign="top">I''m totally surprised this didn''t do better. Really unique composition, I think it was just a bit "muddy" in terms of what was the real subject. I would continue to work on this though, a great idea.<br/> <br/>Jack</td>', 'I''m totally surprised this didn''t do better. Really unique composition, I think it was just a bit "muddy" in terms of what was the real subject. I would continue to work on this though, a great idea. Jack', '2007-02-07 20:11:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341394, 459850, 14620, '<td valign="top">Hmph!  Well, I loved it. :)</td>', 'Hmph!  Well, I loved it. :)', '2007-02-07 20:23:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341405, 461544, 57882, '<td valign="top">Nice control, and amazing color.  Well done.</td>', 'Nice control, and amazing color.  Well done.', '2007-02-07 20:25:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341473, 461298, 28710, '<td valign="top">Easily one of the best shots I''ve ever seen here on DPC.</td>', 'Easily one of the best shots I''ve ever seen here on DPC.', '2007-02-07 20:46:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341483, 461664, 23484, '<td valign="top">I like the way only one small part is in focus and the rest just fades back into nothing.  The blue background really enhances the overall soft feeling to this image. Good job.</td>', 'I like the way only one small part is in focus and the rest just fades back into nothing.  The blue background really enhances the overall soft feeling to this image. Good job.', '2007-02-07 20:48:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341541, 460457, 60915, '<td valign="top">This has a real cubism feel! Very creative! I like that you included some background, it gives the shot some depth. I love the B&amp;W and the noise/grain. Well done! :)</td>', 'This has a real cubism feel! Very creative! I like that you included some background, it gives the shot some depth. I love the B&W and the noise/grain. Well done! :)', '2007-02-07 21:05:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341544, 459778, 62318, '<td valign="top">Great stunning picture. How many takes did it take you to get this depth right, or did you use a depth of field preview button? Love the contrast and the repeating patterns. A wonderful shot with a nice balance throughout the frame.</td>', 'Great stunning picture. How many takes did it take you to get this depth right, or did you use a depth of field preview button? Love the contrast and the repeating patterns. A wonderful shot with a nice balance throughout the frame.', '2007-02-07 21:06:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341557, 461433, 62318, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea, because normally you wouldn''t see the tail coming towards you run out of depth. It looks like some mid-day harsh light coming down on this one? Have you tried a B&amp;W version, sometimes the high contrast works well there. Just a thought. You have the little guy in such a great pose. Sharpness on the central head is good. Maybe a little further crop. This picture is better than the indicated score and a good find on wildlife, those little guys can be such a dasher.</td>', 'Interesting idea, because normally you wouldn''t see the tail coming towards you run out of depth. It looks like some mid-day harsh light coming down on this one? Have you tried a B&W version, sometimes the high contrast works well there. Just a thought. You have the little guy in such a great pose. Sharpness on the central head is good. Maybe a little further crop. This picture is better than the indicated score and a good find on wildlife, those little guys can be such a dasher.', '2007-02-07 21:09:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341674, 459529, 69407, '<td valign="top">This is a stunning photo! Alicia must be really pleased... I can see the shallow DOF, too... I thought this was going to do very well.</td>', 'This is a stunning photo! Alicia must be really pleased... I can see the shallow DOF, too... I thought this was going to do very well.', '2007-02-07 21:45:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3341810, 461298, 51638, '<td valign="top">Amazing capture! Simply amazing.</td>', 'Amazing capture! Simply amazing.', '2007-02-07 22:29:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3342419, 461544, 34763, '<td valign="top">You''ve got the top 20 pretty well nailed. Looks like spring time already Well done!</td>', 'You''ve got the top 20 pretty well nailed. Looks like spring time already Well done!', '2007-02-08 00:27:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3342629, 458116, 60862, '<td valign="top">Very pretty, Catherine.  I like your title, too.</td>', 'Very pretty, Catherine.  I like your title, too.', '2007-02-08 01:41:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3342672, 459473, 60862, '<td valign="top">Great colors!  I wonder how it''d look cropped so that the upper right corner and right edge are all within the right-hand red leg?  Maybe put the top just below the lighter-colored crosspiece?  That way you''d have solid red framing the Space Needle.</td>', 'Great colors!  I wonder how it''d look cropped so that the upper right corner and right edge are all within the right-hand red leg?  Maybe put the top just below the lighter-colored crosspiece?  That way you''d have solid red framing the Space Needle.', '2007-02-08 01:55:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3342679, 460890, 60862, '<td valign="top">Without tipping the domino out, this is just another example showing what DOF means.  With that tipped tile, though, you tell a story and it''s 100 times more interesting.  Congrats!</td>', 'Without tipping the domino out, this is just another example showing what DOF means.  With that tipped tile, though, you tell a story and it''s 100 times more interesting.  Congrats!', '2007-02-08 01:58:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3342681, 459969, 60862, '<td valign="top">Mary, the DOF is nice here, as is the color.  But something about it strikes me as a study of how to shoot narrow DOF as opposed to a subject or presentation that grabs me and makes me look longer.  Look at several of the top 10s, including 1st and 3rd.  The DOF makes us look at something that tells a story.</td>', 'Mary, the DOF is nice here, as is the color.  But something about it strikes me as a study of how to shoot narrow DOF as opposed to a subject or presentation that grabs me and makes me look longer.  Look at several of the top 10s, including 1st and 3rd.  The DOF makes us look at something that tells a story.', '2007-02-08 01:58:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3342751, 460880, 36956, '<td valign="top">splartz argt gache mucha q urtz.  <br/> <br/>I like this... should have scored higher... perhaps not enough burning.  BURN more .... BURN.<br/> <br/>lates bud.<br/> <br/>mH.</td>', 'splartz argt gache mucha q urtz.   I like this... should have scored higher... perhaps not enough burning.  BURN more .... BURN. lates bud. mH.', '2007-02-08 02:32:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3342936, 461355, 72339, '<td valign="top">awesome shot. well done</td>', 'awesome shot. well done', '2007-02-08 04:48:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3342963, 461544, 52549, '<td valign="top">Sandy, I love your "buried in mediocrity" understatement ;-) This image is so beautiful and a well deserved top 20.</td>', 'Sandy, I love your "buried in mediocrity" understatement ;-) This image is so beautiful and a well deserved top 20.', '2007-02-08 05:17:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3343176, 461646, 25355, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting, not so keen on the tilting (but that''s just me).</td>', 'I like the lighting, not so keen on the tilting (but that''s just me).', '2007-02-08 07:53:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(3343312, 459248, 51538, '<td valign="top">Lovely rendition of a teasel.  You have some good photo locations in that part of the world.</td>', 'Lovely rendition of a teasel.  You have some good photo locations in that part of the world.', '2007-02-08 09:06:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3343394, 461693, 30049, '<td valign="top">Hmmm.  Not sure why this didn''t score a little higher.  Maybe it was that the viewers couldn''t engage with the subject, or didn''t see any "Wow" in it?<br/> <br/>Personally I like the balance of the composition and the DOF is on the mark for the challenge.  White balance, focus, lighting, etc... are all fine as well.  Maybe the white cup in between the two blue ones is too much?  Throws off the symetry a little?  Just a thought.<br/> <br/>Smile and keep having fun!</td>', 'Hmmm.  Not sure why this didn''t score a little higher.  Maybe it was that the viewers couldn''t engage with the subject, or didn''t see any "Wow" in it? Personally I like the balance of the composition and the DOF is on the mark for the challenge.  White balance, focus, lighting, etc... are all fine as well.  Maybe the white cup in between the two blue ones is too much?  Throws off the symetry a little?  Just a thought. Smile and keep having fun!', '2007-02-08 09:30:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3343509, 460994, 64733, '<td valign="top">this is a great composition, but a little "soft" as they say.  the focus on the central part of the image just isn''t perfect.</td>', 'this is a great composition, but a little "soft" as they say.  the focus on the central part of the image just isn''t perfect.', '2007-02-08 10:05:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3343581, 461298, 59029, '<td valign="top">What an amazing shot - I can only dream of getting a pic like this!</td>', 'What an amazing shot - I can only dream of getting a pic like this!', '2007-02-08 10:32:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344282, 461693, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals:  I like bounce flash so I think your lighting is excellent.  Your composition is nice with the slightly off centered foreground subject.  The color scheme works well.<br/> <br/>The feel: What are you trying to accomplish here?  This is where the picture fails.  The title gives us the impression we should be "overloaded" either literally or virtually in one of our senses.  Visually, the picture is more bare than crowdede.  We could imagine an overload of coffee smell (mmmmm), but not in this picture.  I can hardly see the coffee and it is trapped in the sterile cage of a white filter.  The DOF, while nicely done, also does not add much here other than to meet the challenge.<br/> <br/>The game: you were rewarded with a near five because your techincals were well done.  You were not rewarded with a higher score because the picture fails for the reasons above and does not transcend beyond an exercise in shallow DOF.</td>', 'The technicals:  I like bounce flash so I think your lighting is excellent.  Your composition is nice with the slightly off centered foreground subject.  The color scheme works well. The feel: What are you trying to accomplish here?  This is where the picture fails.  The title gives us the impression we should be "overloaded" either literally or virtually in one of our senses.  Visually, the picture is more bare than crowdede.  We could imagine an overload of coffee smell (mmmmm), but not in this picture.  I can hardly see the coffee and it is trapped in the sterile cage of a white filter.  The DOF, while nicely done, also does not add much here other than to meet the challenge. The game: you were rewarded with a near five because your techincals were well done.  You were not rewarded with a higher score because the picture fails for the reasons above and does not transcend beyond an exercise in shallow DOF.', '2007-02-08 13:03:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344350, 458223, 40718, '<td valign="top">Short comment because you are over 5.5<br/> <br/>The picture works with the DOF and color contrasts, but the long stem without leaves, while going with your title, isn''t that appealing to me.</td>', 'Short comment because you are over 5.5 The picture works with the DOF and color contrasts, but the long stem without leaves, while going with your title, isn''t that appealing to me.', '2007-02-08 13:19:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344492, 461355, 58728, '<td valign="top">Amazing shot.  Congrats to you!!!</td>', 'Amazing shot.  Congrats to you!!!', '2007-02-08 14:00:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344573, 461355, 14476, '<td valign="top">Giorgio!<br/>Congratulations on a splendid image.  How wonderful to open DPC, in one of my rare computer forays, and find your image on the front page in such a prominent spot.  <br/> <br/>It''s just beautiful.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Giorgio!Congratulations on a splendid image.  How wonderful to open DPC, in one of my rare computer forays, and find your image on the front page in such a prominent spot.   It''s just beautiful. Alice', '2007-02-08 14:21:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344852, 461405, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals: I like the composition of the two geese.  The balance each other well while maintaining interest with asymmetry.  The lighting is flat which doesn''t lead to a very dynamic feel.<br/> <br/>The feel: the DOF is a good idea, but not necessarily with the clutter of the background.  This picture would have been much stronger without the black railing or the boats(?).<br/> <br/>The score: I think you did fairly well for the shot.  The limiting factor is the flat light and the background.  You did the best you could for the situation, but there may not have been a 6+ picture available to take.</td>', 'The technicals: I like the composition of the two geese.  The balance each other well while maintaining interest with asymmetry.  The lighting is flat which doesn''t lead to a very dynamic feel. The feel: the DOF is a good idea, but not necessarily with the clutter of the background.  This picture would have been much stronger without the black railing or the boats(?). The score: I think you did fairly well for the shot.  The limiting factor is the flat light and the background.  You did the best you could for the situation, but there may not have been a 6+ picture available to take.', '2007-02-08 15:37:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3344875, 458085, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals: I think well done.  Focus is sharp on the subject, lighting is active and dynamic.  Colors are nice.  DOF is probably on the deep end for what we were trying to get here.  I do like the "flow" of the ducks up to the corner although the orange leg annoys me a bit.  I probably would have desated it a bit.<br/> <br/>The feel: Duck shots.  What are you going to do?  The successful duck shots I''ve seen have been on the minimalistic line.  One problem is that the shot is so familiar.  Not that that is always bad, sometimes capturing a daily scene is excellent, but here I''m not sure what is being said or accomplished in the picture.  I get no direction or feel to it other than a picture of a duck.<br/> <br/>The score: the difference between this being a 5.3 and a 6.3 lies in "wow" and probably in the DOF.  I agree, it isn''t quite shallow enough.</td>', 'The technicals: I think well done.  Focus is sharp on the subject, lighting is active and dynamic.  Colors are nice.  DOF is probably on the deep end for what we were trying to get here.  I do like the "flow" of the ducks up to the corner although the orange leg annoys me a bit.  I probably would have desated it a bit. The feel: Duck shots.  What are you going to do?  The successful duck shots I''ve seen have been on the minimalistic line.  One problem is that the shot is so familiar.  Not that that is always bad, sometimes capturing a daily scene is excellent, but here I''m not sure what is being said or accomplished in the picture.  I get no direction or feel to it other than a picture of a duck. The score: the difference between this being a 5.3 and a 6.3 lies in "wow" and probably in the DOF.  I agree, it isn''t quite shallow enough.', '2007-02-08 15:43:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3345013, 461664, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think we should dub you Queen of Titles - they''re always so delightfully apt.  I do like this - nice use of the 50mm, and the blue tarp provides a nice background to offset the weed.</td>', 'I think we should dub you Queen of Titles - they''re always so delightfully apt.  I do like this - nice use of the 50mm, and the blue tarp provides a nice background to offset the weed.', '2007-02-08 16:18:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3345017, 461355, 34938, '<td valign="top">conrats on the ribbon on a great image George...I love the background and the slight vignetting...the colours really POP</td>', 'conrats on the ribbon on a great image George...I love the background and the slight vignetting...the colours really POP', '2007-02-08 16:19:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3345061, 461413, 42181, '<td valign="top">Mak,<br/> <br/>I can''t believe it, you beat me by 3 places in this challenge.<br/>Well done sir ;-)<br/> <br/>Bob</td>', 'Mak, I can''t believe it, you beat me by 3 places in this challenge.Well done sir ;-) Bob', '2007-02-08 16:33:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3345213, 461649, 47274, '<td valign="top">love it.</td>', 'love it.', '2007-02-08 17:20:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(3345401, 461451, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals:  Lighting is harsh, which is usual for a brightly lit snow day.  Composition isn''t too bad.<br/> <br/>The feel: although you capture a decent DOF, I''m not sure what the background people are adding to the shot.  In fact, they serve as a distraction to pull our eye away from the subject.  The usual purpose of a shallow DOF is to make the subject stand out.  The people work counter to this.<br/> <br/>The game: I think the picture is a victim of the lighting and the "snapshot" feel.  The background is to blame for this.</td>', 'The technicals:  Lighting is harsh, which is usual for a brightly lit snow day.  Composition isn''t too bad. The feel: although you capture a decent DOF, I''m not sure what the background people are adding to the shot.  In fact, they serve as a distraction to pull our eye away from the subject.  The usual purpose of a shallow DOF is to make the subject stand out.  The people work counter to this. The game: I think the picture is a victim of the lighting and the "snapshot" feel.  The background is to blame for this.', '2007-02-08 18:36:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3345520, 461298, 50695, '<td valign="top">I don''t know how this is shallow dof, but it is a truly remarkable capture. congratulations.</td>', 'I don''t know how this is shallow dof, but it is a truly remarkable capture. congratulations.', '2007-02-08 19:16:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3345523, 459794, 50695, '<td valign="top">wow. you''re getting to be experimental! I''m keeping an eye on you...</td>', 'wow. you''re getting to be experimental! I''m keeping an eye on you...', '2007-02-08 19:18:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3345536, 461326, 50695, '<td valign="top">wow! what a phenomenal image! I wish you''d write some kind of description. I have trouble even imagining how you took this.</td>', 'wow! what a phenomenal image! I wish you''d write some kind of description. I have trouble even imagining how you took this.', '2007-02-08 19:21:28.000000', NULL, 0),
